# PROVIDER-EVIDENCE-CONTROL-CHARACTER-UNSETTLEABLE-2026-09-13 dispositions.
#
# Six provider-evidence encoders emitted a character the Provider Worker's own
# validator refuses, so three observations could never settle and three settled
# only when they had nothing to report. The superseded bytes are frozen beside
# this file because Sprint 4.99 deletes the encoders that produced them, and
# Standard P requires both sides to stay auditable after that deletion.
#
# The refusal cause is the same for all six and is not restated here: the
# expected-failure result is whatever validateProviderIntentEvidence returns for
# the producer's own intent, compared against its published wording.

format-version 1
fixture-id PROVIDER-EVIDENCE-CONTROL-CHARACTER-UNSETTLEABLE-2026-09-13
superseded-result control-character-refused expected-failure
replacement-result canonical-evidence-admitted expected-pass

producer native-stack-family separator newline always-refused
producer eks-iam-role-family separator newline always-refused
producer owned-resource-tags separator tab-and-newline always-refused
producer eks-lbc-family separator newline refused-when-present
producer validation-hosted-zones separator newline refused-when-non-empty
producer dns01-challenge-records separator newline refused-when-non-empty

# The terminal audit is the one producer a separator repair alone could not have
# reached: at a hundred pages its listing cannot fit the 4,096-character wire
# bound in any encoding, and it declared no bound of its own to notice.
bound owned-resource-tags superseded none-declared
bound owned-resource-tags replacement derived-from-character-bound
bound native-stack-family superseded 131072-bytes-and-4096-identities
bound native-stack-family replacement derived-from-character-bound

# Retained-record safety. For every intent in this family no AuthorityProviderCompleted
# record can exist, because its evidence was never admissible; the defect is what
# makes the wire-shape change byte-safe.
retained-record every-producer none-possible
